  "gotchas": [
    {
      "title": "Not 5 V tolerant",
      "text": "GPIO is 3.3 V and the RP2040's absolute maximum on an I/O pin is IOVDD + 0.5 V, so 5 V logic can damage it; use a level shifter.",
      "source": "rp2040-datasheet"
    },
    {
      "title": "ADC accuracy limits",
      "text": "The RP2040 ADC's differential non-linearity peaks at four codes (512, 1536, 2560 and 3584), erratum RP2040-E11, which is not fixed, and its reference comes from the noisy 3.3 V supply. For better accuracy, fit an external reference on ADC_VREF or use an external ADC.",
      "source": "rp2040-datasheet"
    },
    {
      "title": "GP25 is the LED",
      "text": "On the Pico the on-board LED is GPIO25. The Pico W drives its LED from the wireless chip instead, so LED code is not interchangeable between them.",
      "source": "pico-datasheet"
    }
  ],
